### First run: python3 scripts/demo.py seed. These requests reuse the script's stable identities.
@base = http://localhost:8081

### Approved order: COMPLETED, available=8, reserved=2
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: flowops-demo-v1-approved

{"customerId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007","currency":"EUR","items":[{"productId":"flowops-demo-v1-approved","quantity":2,"unitPrice":12.50}]}

### Insufficient stock: CANCELLED without payment
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: flowops-demo-v1-insufficient

{"customerId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007","currency":"EUR","items":[{"productId":"flowops-demo-v1-insufficient","quantity":2,"unitPrice":12.50}]}

### Simulated decline: RELEASING_INVENTORY then CANCELLED, available=5, reserved=0
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: flowops-demo-v1-declined

{"customerId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007","currency":"EUR","items":[{"productId":"flowops-demo-v1-declined","quantity":1,"unitPrice":1001.00}]}

### List the fictitious customer's durable results
GET {{base}}/api/orders?customerId=00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007&size=20
